    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (23 tests, 0 failures) with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment feature following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring Boot app:\n\n**Value logic** \u2014 `membershipNumber` is `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year, zero-padded (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`). It's derived from the owner's own already-assigned fields, so it's seed-independent.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field (mapped to `membership_number`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `assignMembershipNumber(owner)` and wired it into `addOwner` *after* `assignCustomerCode` and the registration-date default (both of which it depends on). MapStruct maps the new field into `OwnerDto` by name automatically.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated DTO carries it).\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `membership_number` column so the persisted value survives the re-read the tests do via `GET`.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests`, the related `Cp07`/`Cp09` tests, and the entire suite are green.",
